  "notes": "Availability zones are tested only as >=2 distinct values. The artifact bucket itself is not created by the ground truth (only its key), and the prompt asks for the key, so no bucket check is written. 'Private' is tested as subnets not auto-assigning public IPs; whether a subnet routes to an internet gateway spans three resources and cannot be expressed in one check. EnableDnsSupport may be omitted, since a VPC has DNS support by default; only an explicit false fails. The ALB and Lambda subnet roles have no resource to observe, since the prompt requests neither an ALB nor a function here. | 2026-11-11 audit: the two subnet checks exclude subnets gated by the optional-NAT Condition, so the NAT-hosting public subnet is not counted as a private subnet or as an ALB subnet. An ungated public subnet would still be counted."
